---
/**
 * Privacy notice.
 *
 * Written from what this website actually does, checked against the code:
 * the only thing that leaves the visitor's browser is the contact form
 * (src/scripts/form.ts → api/contact.js); the chatbot answers locally; the
 * site sets no cookies and loads no analytics, advertising or third-party
 * scripts or fonts. If any of that changes, this page must change with it —
 * see docs/claims-register.md.
 *
 * It describes practice; it does not claim compliance with any particular
 * law. Have it reviewed before relying on it for that.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '30 September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What NYT Software Solutions collects through this website, why, who processes it, how long it is kept, and how to reach us about your data."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy notice' }]}
>
  <article class="container legal">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <p class="page-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">
        The short version: this site collects nothing about you unless you
        write to us. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads nothing
        from other companies' servers. When you do write, we use what you send
        to reply to you, and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by {site.legalName}, based in {site.locality},
        {site.country}. For anything about your data, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

      <h3>When you send the contact form</h3>
      <p>
        We receive your name or organisation, your email address, the interest
        area you choose, the budget range and timeline if you give them, and
        your message. We use them to reply to your enquiry and, if it becomes
        a project, to discuss and scope it. You confirm you are happy for us to
        contact you before the form is sent.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also send you an automatic confirmation email containing a copy of
        what you wrote, so you have a record of it.
      </p>

      <h3>When you visit any page</h3>
      <p>
        Like every website, ours receives technical information with each
        request — your IP address, browser type and the page requested — which
        our hosting provider uses to deliver the site and protect it from
        abuse. To stop the contact form being flooded, the server remembers
        the IP address of each submission for up to ten minutes, in memory
        only, and then forgets it.
      </p>

      <h3>What stays in your browser</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your view preference.</strong> If you switch between the
          Business and Engineering views, your choice is saved in your
          browser's local storage (<code>nyt-persona</code>) so the site
          remembers it. It is never sent to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your demo request.</strong> If you click "Request a demo" on
          another page, the choice is kept in session storage just long enough
          to pre-select it in the form, then deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An offline copy.</strong> The site stores copies of its own
          pages and files in your browser so it still opens without a
          connection. They contain nothing about you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can clear all of these at any time from your browser's settings.
        The site uses no cookies, so there is nothing to consent to until you
        choose to send the form.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of service providers to run the site and receive enquiries:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosts the website and the function that receives the contact form.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers the enquiry to us and your confirmation copy to you.</li>
        <li><strong>Google (Gmail)</strong> — hosts our business mailbox, where enquiries arrive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers may process data outside Ethiopia. We do not sell your
        data, share it for advertising, or pass it to anyone else unless the law
        requires us to.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries only for as long as we need them to reply and, if a
        project follows, to carry it out. You can ask us to delete yours at any
        time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us
        to delete it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        We will reply from that address.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If what the site collects changes, this page changes with it, and the
        date at the top is updated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Page>
